<article class="env-definition" id="011N">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/011N">Definition <span data-tag="011N">12.20.1</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
A <em>spectral sequence in $\mathcal{A}$</em> is given by a system $(E_ r, d_ r)_{r \geq 1}$ where each $E_ r$ is an object of $\mathcal{A}$, each $d_ r : E_ r \to E_ r$ is a morphism such that $d_ r \circ d_ r = 0$ and $E_{r + 1} = \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(d_ r)/\mathop{\mathrm{Im}}(d_ r)$ for $r \geq 1$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
A <em>morphism of spectral sequences</em> $f : (E_ r, d_ r)_{r \geq 1} \to (E'_ r, d'_ r)_{r \geq 1}$ is given by a family of morphisms $f_ r : E_ r \to E'_ r$ such that $f_ r \circ d_ r = d'_ r \circ f_ r$ and such that $f_{r + 1}$ is the morphism induced by $f_ r$ via the identifications $E_{r + 1} = \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(d_ r)/\mathop{\mathrm{Im}}(d_ r)$ and $E'_{r + 1} = \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(d'_ r)/\mathop{\mathrm{Im}}(d'_ r)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>